  "reply_markdown": "**Q1. Compatibility.** I found two additional problems in the Claude transcript guard: a valid Unicode path can panic (finding #1), and the derived path omits the NFC normalization described in the implementation notes (finding #2). Neither is identified as an intentional difference. The documented endpoint preflight remains a version probe, not proof that `-p` works; F32-1 is therefore only partially resolved.\n\n**Q2. Going beyond the plugin.** The complaint locking and identity recheck address the inspected deletion race. The journal extension preserves C3's replay decisions, but does not establish once-only replay across both bridges: `wave2b-compat.md:390–417` explicitly reports that plugin 0.6.1 re-adds marked, evicted records. F29-1 remains open for that shared invariant; this is a documented plugin limitation, not evidence of a newly broken file format.\n\nThe pre-kill record improves the successful-write path, but F30-2 remains open when persistence fails. `before_kill` stores the write error in memory and returns no result; `kill_tree_checked` proceeds unconditionally. The existing write-failure test explicitly expects the surviving record to remain `running`, naming only the child. A subsequent refusal to commit does not restore evidence lost if the bridge dies during that interval. F23-3 consequently remains open for this failure schedule.\n\nI did not independently validate the full-roster plan change or all interchange paths.\n\n**Q3. P7/P8.** Acceptable as explicit release boundaries: independent telemetry identities/outboxes in production, and sequential oracle adaptation in test mode. P8 does not support concurrent plugin/C3 access to the redirected files; its documentation acknowledges different lock domains. C3 tests can replace path-specific telemetry assertions, but expected failure counts alone cannot certify semantic equivalence. The reported 772 tests and live runs are useful evidence, not tests I reran. The named live matrix provides no demonstrated Claude `api-key` run.\n\n**Q4. Verdict.** **HOLD; do not tag yet.** Acceptance blockers are finding #1 and F30-2. Address finding #2 and reconcile the remaining shared-journal guarantee with F29-1 before claiming all findings closed. F32-1's documented probe limitation should likewise remain explicit rather than marked completely fixed.\n\nThis was a bounded, read-only review using 12 tool calls, without agents, builds, live requests, or edits. I read selected sections of every named wave document, the state, RC2/RC3/RC5/RC6 reports, README and changelog, then targeted code and test ranges. HEAD is newer than the target; the comparison showed no subsequent changes under `crates`, README or CHANGELOG, and only the added RC6 report under the inspected documentation paths. I did not read the complete 220-file delta, consultation archives, complete test bodies, raw verification logs, most orchestration/engine/panel/ledger changes, or the complete shim coverage inventory. `not-checked` entries are not closure endorsements.\n\n## Requested checks\n\n- **RC1 — finding #1:** Working directory `C:\\Users\\Dmytro\\C3`; workspace-write; add and run a Windows regression calling `launch_problem_of` with root `C:\\repo`, `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=C:\\日本\\.claude`, and no reported projects directory. Require normal return, without panic. Budget: one targeted test, 10 minutes.\n- **RC2 — F30-2:** Same working directory; workspace-write; extend the existing read-only-pending-file fixture to pause immediately after killing, terminate the bridge there, restore file access and attempt recovery with a surviving helper. Require durable blocking evidence and refusal of a new turn. Budget: one deterministic fixture, 20 minutes.\n- **RC3 — finding #2:** Same working directory; workspace-write; create a scratch repository whose final component is NFC `café`, pass its decomposed equivalent as `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, and test endpoint preflight with a fake launcher. Require refusal before a turn. Budget: one fixture, 10 minutes.\n- **RC4 — F29-1:** Same working directory; workspace-write; replay the documented retained-journal/500-record-cap schedule through two consecutive pinned-plugin updates followed by C3. Require no resurrection or displacement, or explicitly record this invariant as unsupported with plugin 0.6.1. Budget: one isolated health directory, 15 minutes.",
